In strict one-action puzzle interfaces, the protocol remains binding after the puzzle ends. When feedback says the instance is over—especially after exhausting the attempt cap—respond with exactly `{"action":"finish"}`. An empty assistant response or another `submit` is not a valid terminal action.

After a wrong submission, binary feedback gives no location information. Do not respond with a cosmetic or arbitrary variant (for example, changing only a suspected region's color). State the proposed model correction internally and test it against the complete demonstrations, including unchanged pairs and preserved cells. Only submit when the revised rule has evidence and reproduces all examples. If ambiguity remains and a demo is available, request one only to resolve a specific competing hypothesis; once demos are exhausted, further unsupported guesses compound cost and risk consuming the cap.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-rnd0/frozen/seen/play/users/u059/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-puzzle-solving/references/attempt-cap-and-retry-gate.md"}
